      "html": "<ol><li><strong>Carry on as normal.</strong> Answer by voice note, text or photo as you walk. Your phone holds what it could not send.</li><li><strong>Say done when you are done.</strong> Type or say done at the end of the walk, even if you have no signal yet. A done that reaches Quickler before the rest of your messages is still read as the end of that walk.</li><li><strong>Signal returns, the burst arrives.</strong> WhatsApp delivers the queue. Messages that arrive close together, each within 90 seconds of the one before, are one walk. They may land out of order, and Quickler copes.</li><li><strong>Voice notes and photos catch up.</strong> Voice notes are written out as they arrive. Photos are placed on the right question once you have said done.</li><li><strong>Quickler replies.</strong> After each message Quickler sends a status: what is covered, what still needs covering and how many photos it holds. When signal returns, those replies arrive too.</li></ol>"
